      "content": "I understand your concern about kidney stones and desire to improve your health. However, consuming an unusually high amount of vitamin C, especially 2500 mg daily, is not recommended and can have negative side effects, including the development of kidney stones and other issues. It’s important to consult with a healthcare professional before making any major changes to your diet or supplement intake. They can provide personalized advice and provide safer alternatives to manage your health concerns.",
